<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argyll</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Argyll is a region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, made up of sea lochs, peninsulas and islands, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kintyre">Kintyre</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cowal">Cowal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorn">Lorn</a>. Its name means 'coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaels">Gaels</a>'. It was the British territory of the early medieval kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a> and later the base of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerled">Somerled</a>'s Kingdom of the Isles and of the Campbell earls and dukes of Argyll.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argyll.jpg" alt="Argyll" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: OwenBlacker, updated by Elianfoo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Argyllshire_locator_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
